From 28d5e0d22491b1cc73283b9189c0716534b87754 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: justinasvijeikis <80092258+justinasvijeikis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:09:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Debian: macOS Escape, GNOME theme, user themes and Fn
 chords

- Escape is 64 pt like macOS; F1-F12 share the rest.
- Follow GNOME accent and light/dark style via gsettings monitor.
- touchbar.conf: built-in default/penguin themes, user themes with PNG
  background, watermark, mascot and Fn icons; hot reload.
- Dependency-free PNG decoder for theme art.
- TapKeys emits one chord (pressed in order, released in reverse) over a
  fixed 101-key allowlist shared by wire.rs and the native uinput table.
- Fn keys can run a key chord or a command.
- debian/: desktop provider (wpctl, MPRIS), installer incl. usbmuxd udev
  fix and user config, README.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
